{"whyItMatters":"Minor bug-fix release of a GitHub login plugin for Datasette fixing cookie expiration issues.","corroborationToday":1,"section":"ai","gsi1pk":"DAY#2026-09-20","pk":"ART#5d4229283cd8263c0fb9a199eb5fb9cc48ea0f263b81491422f607dbe63452ed","gsi1sk":"0349#5d4229283cd8263c0fb9a199eb5fb9cc48ea0f263b81491422f607dbe63452ed","sourceName":"Simon Willison","publishedAt":"2026-09-19T19:52:02.000Z","source":"simonwillison","scoreVersion":"v1","firstSeenAt":"2026-09-19T22:08:36.210Z","url":"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Sep/19/datasette-auth-github","llmImportance":10,"sk":"A","title":"datasette-auth-github 1.0","summary":"Release: datasette-auth-github 1.0 I run this GitHub login plugin on the agent.datasette.io demo site and I noticed that my authenticated sessions weren't lasting very long. It turned out that the plugin was setting cookies without a Max-Age parameter, so they were expiring at the end of a browser session (which in Mobile Safari seems to happen pretty often, independently of how you are using the app.) I fixed that in #80 and, since this plugin has been around for quite a while and is tested against both Datasette 0.65.x and Datasette 1.0ax, I decided to bump it up to a 1.0 release. I'm trying","score":348.5258860893122,"pointsImputed":true,"clusterId":"2026-09-20#datasette-auth-github-release","category":"community"}
